  "discovery": {
    "citation": "Claudine Madras Gartenberg (b. 1975) is an American professor of management at the University of Pennsylvania.  As a high-school scientist, she performed light-curve measurements of asteroid (951) Gaspra, deducing its rotation period and shape in advance of the 1991 Galileo spacecraft flyby.  Her asteroid work was recognized by a 1992 Westinghouse Prize.",
